    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d270">

                <pb facs="0489" n="427" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg427"/>

                <head>No. 265.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Langston to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince, Hayti</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-01-09"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 9, 1878</date>.
                        (Received January 25.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 21.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have heretofore, as an inclosure to my
                    No. 16, transmitted a copy of the dispatch of the Hon. Felix Carrié, Secretary
                    of State for Foreign Affairs, dated December 13, 1877, having reference to the
                    imposition of one per centum on invoices of merchandise shipped from the United
                    States to the ports of this republic. I have the honor to transmit herein
                    inclosed a copy of my reply thereto, and to state that I await the answer of the
                    Haytian Government; as soon as it is received, I shall transmit it.</p>
                <p>With sentiments, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN MERCER LANGSTON.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d270-a1.xml" xpointer="d270-a1"/>
            </div>
